Question 1: Determine which of the following five relations defined on Z are equivalence relations:
(a) {(a,b) ∈ Z x Z: (a > 0 and b > 0) or (a < 0 and b < 0)}
(b) {(a,b) ∈ Z x Z: (a > 0 and b > 0) or (a < 0 and b < 0)}
(c) {(a,b) ∈ Z x Z: |a - b| < 10}
(d) {(a,b) ∈ Z x Z: (a < 0 and b > 0) or (a < 0 and b < 0)}
(e) {(a,b) ∈ Z x Z: (a > 0 and b > 0) or (a < 0 and b < 0)}

Question 1: Let A = {a, b, c, d}. For each of the following partitions of A, list all the pairs of elements that form the corresponding equivalence relations:
(a) {{a, b, c}, {d}}
(b) {{a}, {b}, {c}, {d}}
(c) {{a, b, c, d}}

Question 2: Let A = {a, b, c, d}. For each of the following partitions of A, determine the elements of the corresponding equivalence relation:
(a) P1 = {{a, c}, {b, d}}
(b) P2 = {{a}, {b, c}, {d}}
(c) P3 = {{a, b}, {c, d}}
(d) P4 = {{a, b, c}, {d}}
Do any of these partitions refine any of the others?

Question 2: Draw a diagram to represent the I (divides) partial order on the following:
(a) {1, 11}
(b) {1, 3, 7, 21}
(c) {1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12, 18, 36}
(d) {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}
